From 4f6158c819221fecd36216f74b206abebb3b5c31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yun Dou <dixyes@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:11:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] arm64: Take the mmap lock again when a fault gives it up

get_user_pages_remote() works with the mapping lock held, and hands it
back when the fault that makes the page writable has to wait. The caller
learns that from the value it passes in and out: it comes back zero when
the lock is not held, which is what a signal taken while it waited
leaves behind.

The loop here took the next round without it -- looking the mapping up
and calling in again while saying the lock was held -- and unlocked at
the end anyway. That leaves the mm's lock count wrong: the next caller
that checks it is warned at, and a reader can be left waiting for an
owner that is not there. A machine with rcpc_rewrite on was seen to do
exactly that, with a task stuck in the block fault hook for over two
minutes.

Take it again before the next try, and stop after a few rather than
spin. Nothing depends on the rewrite but speed: the caller carries the
instruction out either way.

Assisted-by: dsh:DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash
(cherry picked from commit 0349bb4d97fac755be015ec1bf56a5e94fa5c2a7)
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/undef_patch.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/undef_patch.c b/arch/arm64/kernel/undef_patch.c
index ff4032b3e0bb..06375dfd927c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/undef_patch.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/undef_patch.c
@@ -22,6 +22,9 @@
 #include <asm/sysreg.h>
 #include <asm/traps.h>
 
+/* How many times a fault that takes the lock away is retried */
+#define UNDEF_PATCH_TRIES	8
+
 /*
  * Whether an unaligned atomic access is allowed here, which is what
  * ID_AA64MMFR2_EL1.AT reports: without ARMv8.4-LSE, an atomic access and a
@@ -94,10 +97,11 @@ bool undef_patch_text(struct pt_regs *regs, u32 insn, u32 replacement)
 	bool patched = false;
 	void *kaddr;
 	int locked;
+	int tries;
 	long ret;
 
 	mmap_read_lock(current->mm);
-	for (;;) {
+	for (tries = 0; tries < UNDEF_PATCH_TRIES; tries++) {
 		vma = vma_lookup(current->mm, pc);
 		if (!vma || !(vma->vm_flags & VM_EXEC) ||
 		    (vma->vm_flags & VM_SHARED)) {
@@ -110,7 +114,22 @@ bool undef_patch_text(struct pt_regs *regs, u32 insn, u32 replacement)
 					    gup_flags, &page, &locked);
 		if (locked)
 			break;
-		/* the mapping may have been replaced while the page faulted */
+
+		/*
+		 * The lock is dropped around the fault that makes the page
+		 * writable, and a signal taken while it faults can leave it
+		 * dropped: that is what handing back unlocked as zero says.
+		 * Take it again, because the mapping above is only good
+		 * under it, and give up rather than spin if it keeps
+		 * happening
+		 */
+		mmap_read_lock(current->mm);
+	}
+
+	if (tries == UNDEF_PATCH_TRIES) {
+		mmap_read_unlock(current->mm);
+
+		return false;
 	}
 
 	if (ret == 1) {
